    {
      "version": "v1.1",
      "date": "2026-10-06",
      "summary": "v1.1 — the single bump planned in core worklist item 4, cut from the 2026-10-06 decision set (Decisions 35–43). Solution keeps only class-level properties and binds to a new governed solution-concepts vocabulary; deployment context moves to Action and to the asserting edges (IMPLEMENTS, TARGETS, FACES, EXPERIENCES, PRESCRIBES); Action no longer needs a parent Plan, gains equity_focus / target_populations / is_pilot / alternative_names, and its status (with every other progress-type property) becomes a dated observation series with defined values; plan goal wording lives in local_label on SETS / PURSUES / PRESCRIBES; the finance model is rebuilt around a FundingAllocation node with two comparison axes (source_tier, instrument_class), FinancingSource becomes FundingStream, FUNDED_BY / CHANNELS_THROUGH are retired. The hazard vocabulary is unchanged: no flood parent term, and the urban heat island is not a hazard (Decision 42). An Action or CapitalProject can be DEPLOYED_IN a named Place, and a capital project's outcomes go through the Action it realizes (Decision 44).",
      "changes": [
        {
          "type": "added",
          "text": "FundingAllocation type; FUNDS, PROVIDED_BY, ADMINISTERED_BY, ISSUED_BY edges; USES_INSTRUMENT retargeted to FundingAllocation (Decision 43)"
        },
        {
          "type": "changed",
          "text": "FinancingSource → FundingStream; source_type → stream_type; amount_usd replaced by max_award (Decision 43)"
        },
        {
          "type": "removed",
          "text": "FUNDED_BY (Action, CapitalProject), USES_INSTRUMENT (Action, CapitalProject), CHANNELS_THROUGH; FinancialInstrument.amount_usd and .issuer (Decision 43)"
        },
        {
          "type": "added",
          "text": "enums: source_tier, instrument_class, funding_status, amount_qualifier, stream_type; instrument_type + loan, tax_abatement, insurance, ground_lease; financing_model deprecated with a value map (Decision 43)"
        },
        {
          "type": "added",
          "text": "vocabularies/solution-concepts.json (101 concepts, v0, reviewed) bound to Solution.concept_id; solution-categories + governance_and_policy category (5 subcategories) and 4 non-tech subcategories elsewhere, 92 → 101 (Decision 35)"
        },
        {
          "type": "removed",
          "text": "Solution.year_of_deployment, maturity_level, equity_focus, target_populations; category_id no longer required — category_id, subcategory_id, ipcc_action_types are derived from concept_id (Decision 35)"
        },
        {
          "type": "changed",
          "text": "Solution and Action definitions and extract hints: a named programme is an Action; an Action needs no parent Plan (Decisions 35, 39)"
        },
        {
          "type": "added",
          "text": "Action.equity_focus, Action.target_populations (Decision 36); Action.alternative_names, Plan.alternative_names, Action.is_pilot (Decision 39)"
        },
        {
          "type": "changed",
          "text": "Action.status and PRESCRIBES.implementation_stage share enums.action_status with definitions; + not_started, on_hold (Decision 39)"
        },
        {
          "type": "added",
          "text": "*_observations dated series on Action.status, Action.financing_status, CapitalProject.construction_phase / financing_status, Plan.plan_status, PRESCRIBES.implementation_stage, FundingAllocation.funding_status; Plan.plan_status becomes an enum (Decision 40)"
        },
        {
          "type": "changed",
          "text": "UrbanSystem.condition/capacity/service_coverage → TARGETS; Barrier.severity_score/affected_stakeholder → FACES; Vulnerability scores → EXPERIENCES; IMPLEMENTS + scale_quantity, scale_unit, is_primary (Decision 37)"
        },
        {
          "type": "added",
          "text": "local_label on PRESCRIBES, SETS, PURSUES, DEMONSTRATES_PROGRESS_ON; CONTRIBUTES_TO.contribution_description restricted to class-level text and its definition's TARGETS_GOAL reference fixed to PURSUES (Decisions 38, 41)"
        },
        {
          "type": "changed",
          "text": "ResilienceGoal extract_hint excludes a plan's own goal numbering and headings; Hazard and relationship hints no longer use the urban heat island as a hazard (Decision 42)"
        },
        {
          "type": "added",
          "text": "DEPLOYED_IN Action → Place and CapitalProject → Place: site-level anchoring (Decision 44, ontology#13)"
        },
        {
          "type": "removed",
          "text": "PRODUCES CapitalProject → Outcome; a project's outcomes go CapitalProject REALIZES Action RESULTS_IN Outcome (Decision 44, ontology#4)"
        },
        {
          "type": "added",
          "text": "claim_ids on REDUCES_EXPOSURE, SHAPES and INFORMS (the three edges that had no provenance property)"
        },
        {
          "type": "added",
          "text": "scripts/export/build_vocab_jsonld.py regenerates the vocabulary .jsonld twins; scripts/migrations/v1_1_from_v1_0.py is the migration"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "version": "v1.0",
      "date": "2026-08-18",
      "summary": "JSON-LD source migration (no ontology schema change from v0.8 — same 21 types, 60 relationships, 48 predicate ids): the ontology's source format is now JSON-LD 1.1 with a shared @context, directly consumable by standard RDF tooling (rdflib, Protege, SPARQL). OWL/Turtle/SKOS exports generate in CI from this source instead of being hand-maintained separately. Two live data bugs found and fixed while building the context; full rationale in Decision 34.",
      "changes": [
        {
          "type": "added",
          "text": "ontology/context.jsonld — shared JSON-LD 1.1 @context; ab: (https://ontology.adaptbase.us/ont/) and abv: (https://ontology.adaptbase.us/vocab/) namespaces"
        },
        {
          "type": "added",
          "text": "@id/@type on every type (owl:Class) and relationship (owl:ObjectProperty); the 10 duplicate-predicate-id groups each gained a specific @id per (source,target) row (e.g. ab:actionDeployedInJurisdiction), linked via rdfs:subPropertyOf to a shared umbrella @id (e.g. ab:deployedIn)"
        },
        {
          "type": "added",
          "text": "ontology/vocabularies/*.jsonld (8 files) — skos:ConceptScheme/skos:Concept typing; enums.json's 20 blocks each get their own scheme id (abv:enums-<block>) instead of one opaque manifest row"
        },
        {
          "type": "added",
          "text": "scripts/export/generate_exports.py — rdflib-based Turtle/OWL/SKOS export, wired into the GitHub Pages CI workflow; exports/ is generated fresh on every deploy, not committed"
        },
        {
          "type": "changed",
          "text": "vocabularies[] manifest expanded from 7 to 27 rows — one row per enums.json block plus the previously-missing jurisdiction-kind, instead of one opaque 'enums' row with bound_to: ['various']"
        },
        {
          "type": "fixed",
          "text": "Outcome.beneficiary_program's stale 'vocabulary': 'enums' pointer (no matching block; values were already inline) — same bug class already fixed once for UrbanSystem in v0.4.1"
        },
        {
          "type": "fixed",
          "text": "USES_INSTRUMENT(CapitalProject).financing_model's malformed 'vocab' key (should have been 'vocabulary_binding') — the viewer's inspector never read that key, so its enum options were silently not rendering"
        },
        {
          "type": "changed",
          "text": "6 properties with 'vocabulary': 'enums' (relying on an unwritten property-id-matches-block-name convention) normalized to explicit vocabulary_binding: {vocab, field}"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "version": "v0.8",
      "date": "2026-08-13",
      "summary": "Catalog-node edge re-anchoring (issue adaptbase-core#170): catalog entities merge by name and are shared across cities, so deployment-context edges on them leak one city's facts into another's two-hop queries. Seven edge rows move to the instance-grain Action; the class-knowledge channels (PRODUCES, IMPLEMENTED_IN, EXPOSES) stay, guarded by precedence rules. Edge count unchanged at 60.",
      "changes": [
        {
          "type": "removed",
          "text": "Solution → USES_INSTRUMENT → FinancialInstrument — financing is one deployment's fact (73 live edges hung off shared Solutions, 33 of 46 financed Solutions span multiple cities)"
        },
        {
          "type": "removed",
          "text": "Solution → IMPLEMENTED_BY → Stakeholder — the name-merged node destroys the boundary between co-implementers of one deployment and unrelated cities' implementers (CapitalProject variant stays)"
        },
        {
          "type": "removed",
          "text": "Solution → GENERATES → PlanningData — every extracted object is a city-specific dataset; the class-level reading is tautological"
        },
        {
          "type": "removed",
          "text": "Solution → REDUCES_EXPOSURE → ExposureUnit — the AR6 triad's only instance-target edge; who-is-protected is a deployment claim"
        },
        {
          "type": "removed",
          "text": "Solution → SHIFTS_RISK_TO → ExposureUnit — mirror of REDUCES_EXPOSURE on the maladaptation side; zero live and staged volume, so re-anchored pre-emptively at zero backfill cost"
        },
        {
          "type": "removed",
          "text": "Stakeholder → PARTICIPATES_IN → Solution — designed partner of IMPLEMENTED_BY; lead and non-lead involvement must sit at the same grain"
        },
        {
          "type": "removed",
          "text": "Supplier → SUPPLIES → Solution — extracted facts are one city's procurement relations, not vendor product lines"
        },
        {
          "type": "added",
          "text": "Action → USES_INSTRUMENT → FinancialInstrument — amount_usd, financing_model, description, claim_ids (no share_percent: an Action has no project-total); completes the action-grain financing triangle with FUNDED_BY"
        },
        {
          "type": "added",
          "text": "Action → IMPLEMENTED_BY → Stakeholder — role/is_lead carried over"
        },
        {
          "type": "added",
          "text": "Action → GENERATES → PlanningData — makes the GENERATES → INFORMS feedback loop a traceable causal chain"
        },
        {
          "type": "added",
          "text": "Action → REDUCES_EXPOSURE → ExposureUnit — instance grain on both ends"
        },
        {
          "type": "added",
          "text": "Action → SHIFTS_RISK_TO → ExposureUnit — mechanism carried over"
        },
        {
          "type": "added",
          "text": "Stakeholder → PARTICIPATES_IN → Action — participation_role carried over"
        },
        {
          "type": "added",
          "text": "Supplier → SUPPLIES → Action — component_refs carried over"
        },
        {
          "type": "changed",
          "text": "PRODUCES (Solution → Outcome) kept as the deliberately class-level channel; extract_hint now rules that measured single-deployment results go to RESULTS_IN from the implementing Action (and RESULTS_IN gets the complementary rule)"
        },
        {
          "type": "changed",
          "text": "IMPLEMENTED_IN (Solution → Jurisdiction) kept — self-contextualizing, the designed replication-tracking channel; extract_hint now prefers Action DEPLOYED_IN when a concrete action exists, and consumers union both paths"
        },
        {
          "type": "changed",
          "text": "EXPOSES (Hazard → ExposureUnit) kept — UNDRR risk-pathway core; LOCATED_IN notes now name it the anchor for city-scoped exposure queries, to be auto-emitted when the source document has a wikidata_qid"
        },
        {
          "type": "changed",
          "text": "Cross-references updated: CapitalProject USES_INSTRUMENT / IMPLEMENTED_BY now mirror the Action variants; PlanningData type notes point at Action GENERATES"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "version": "v0.7",
      "date": "2026-07-07",
      "summary": "Merge GovernanceStructure into Stakeholder. Both definitions claimed named public agencies, causing systematic classifier disagreement in gold annotation, and GovernanceStructure's two-edge topology stranded nodes from actor edges like IMPLEMENTED_BY. Governance is a function, not an identity: it is now expressed via Stakeholder properties and the GOVERNS edge.",
      "changes": [
        {
          "type": "removed",
          "text": "GovernanceStructure type (introduced v0.3) — fully absorbed by Stakeholder"
        },
        {
          "type": "changed",
          "text": "Stakeholder — gains optional org_form (interagency_body / public_agency / advisory_committee / task_force / public_private_partnership / other), authority_level (advisory / regulatory / operational / other), and mandate_description properties; definition and extract hint widened to cover formal governance bodies"
        },
        {
          "type": "changed",
          "text": "GOVERNS (GovernanceStructure → Plan) retargeted to Stakeholder → Plan, alongside the existing GOVERNS (Stakeholder → Jurisdiction) signature"
        },
        {
          "type": "changed",
          "text": "MEMBER_OF (Stakeholder → GovernanceStructure) retargeted to Stakeholder → Stakeholder"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "version": "v0.6.1",
      "date": "2026-07-01",
      "summary": "Add cdp-hazard-crosswalk.json vocabulary, mapping CDP's 23 controlled climate-hazard disclosure values to ontology hazard_ids. Vocabulary/metadata only — no type, relationship, or hazards.json changes.",
      "changes": [
        {
          "type": "added",
          "text": "ontology/vocabularies/cdp-hazard-crosswalk.json — 23 CDP action_hazards_en / goal_hazards controlled values mapped to hazard_ids (17 exact, 4 broader-cluster, 2 ambiguous, 1 partial, 1 gap), plus the 'Action does not address hazard' sentinel documented as excluded"
        },
        {
          "type": "added",
          "text": "vocabularies[] registry entry for cdp-hazard-crosswalk; vocabularies_count 6 → 7"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "version": "v0.6",
      "date": "2026-06-30",
      "summary": "Action-, goal-, and project-level edges for CDP city-action and 2024 fact-table data, and the long-missing FUNDED_BY relationship is finally defined.",
      "changes": [
        {
          "type": "added",
          "text": "ADDRESSES (Action → Hazard) — action-grain hazard link from CDP climate_hazard_s_that_action; reuses the ADDRESSES id alongside Plan → Hazard"
        },
        {
          "type": "added",
          "text": "ADDRESSES (ResilienceGoal → Hazard) — goal-grain hazard target from the 2024 fact-table goal_hazards; reuses the ADDRESSES id"
        },
        {
          "type": "added",
          "text": "TARGETS (Action → UrbanSystem) — action-grain sector/system link from CDP sectors_adaptation_action; reuses the TARGETS id alongside Plan → UrbanSystem"
        },
        {
          "type": "added",
          "text": "TARGETS (CapitalProject → UrbanSystem) — project-grain system domain from CDP project_area; promotes system domain from the asset_class property to a queryable edge"
        },
        {
          "type": "added",
          "text": "FUNDED_BY (Action → FinancingSource) — action-grain funding link from CDP funding_source_s, with amount_usd and claim_ids"
        },
        {
          "type": "fixed",
          "text": "FUNDED_BY (CapitalProject → FinancingSource) defined for the first time — referenced in v0.2's change_history, the 'Resilience Finance — Five-Axis Split' design note, and the CapitalProject USES_INSTRUMENT notes since v0.2 but never present in the relationships array; carries amount_usd, share_percent, and claim_ids"
        },
        {
          "type": "changed",
          "text": "entity notes updated for Action, ResilienceGoal, CapitalProject; 'CapitalProject Edge Economy' design note revised to record the system-domain reversal; new 'Action-level CDP edges & FUNDED_BY landing (v0.6)' design note added"
        },
        {
          "type": "fixed",
          "text": "corrected drifted metadata counts: relationships_count → 60 (the v0.5.1 array already held 54 rows but declared 51; +6 new v0.6 rows = 60) and types_count 21 → 22 (Place, added in v0.5.0, was never counted)"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "version": "v0.4.1",
      "date": "2026-05-14",
      "summary": "Vocabulary alignment sweep — fix enum drift between ontology schema and enums.json, add missing sectors and population types.",
      "changes": [
        {
          "type": "added",
          "text": "EnablingCondition.condition_type: added 'political' (was already present on Barrier.barrier_type)"
        },
        {
          "type": "added",
